    "# Jha et al. (2025), ChatGPT and Corporate Policies\n",
    "### Using an LLM to extract a forward-looking CapEx signal, then testing whether it predicts realized investment\n",
    "\n",
    "**Summer Camp — Short empirical exercise**\n",
    "\n",
    "---\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook walks the pipeline of a modern text-as-data finance study, in miniature:\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Unstructured text** (earnings call transcripts) → **LLM classification** → **structured signal** (−1 … +1) → **link to COMPUSTAT** → **test predictive validity**\n",
    "\n",
    "We use 8 large firms from late-2023 (Oct/Nov) earnings calls across several sectors — Union Pacific, Microsoft, Intel, Amazon, Caterpillar, Pfizer, NextEra/FPL, and NVIDIA — and ask a simple question:\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Does the information in the late 2023 earnings calls predict what they *actually spend* in fiscal 2024?**\n",
    "\n",
    "The exercise is built in three acts. Run the cells in order.\n",
    "\n",
    "**A note on sample size:** with only 8 firms this is a *teaching* dataset, not a result. Treat every p-value as illustration, not evidence.\n"
   ]
  },
