    "---\n",
    "# Act 1: Extraction: can an LLM read an earnings call like an analyst?\n",
    "\n",
    "The raw input is a set of JSON transcript files named by ID (e.g. `2922311.json`). For each one, we send the transcript to the model with a carefully worded prompt and ask it to classify the firm's forward-looking capital-spending plan into one of five categories, **with a one-sentence justification grounded in the text**.\n",
    "\n",
    "These transcript files come from WRDS. The code below shows how to connect to WRDS, from which you can retrieve them directly.\n",
    "\n",
    "The prompt is the heart of this step. Read it carefully, every instruction in it is a research design choice.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "89328908",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "89328908"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "PROMPT_TEMPLATE = \"\"\"The following text is an excerpt from a company\\'s earnings call transcripts. You are a finance expert. Based on this text only, please answer the following question. How does the firm plan to change its capital spending over the next year? There are five choices: Increase substantially, increase, no change, decrease, and decrease substantially. Please select one of the above five choices for each question and provide a one-sentence explanation of your choice for each question. The format for the answer to each question should be \"choice - explanation.\" If no relevant information is provided related to the question, answer \"no information is provided.\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Transcript:\n",
    "{transcript}\"\"\"\n",
    "\n",
    "print(PROMPT_TEMPLATE)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f7453a58",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "f7453a58"
   },
   "source": [
    "### The extraction code\n",
    "\n",
    "This loops over every `.json` file in the folder, pulls out the transcript text, sends it to the model, and writes the results to `capex_forecasts.csv`. The `extract_transcript_text()` helper handles a few common JSON shapes — **you may need to adjust it to match the exact structure of your transcript files.**\n",
    "\n",
    "> ⚠️ **Running this cell makes real API calls and costs a small amount of money.** If you just want to proceed with the analysis, skip ahead — the output `capex_forecasts.csv` is already provided.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "9027d414",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "9027d414"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import anthropic\n",
    "\n",
    "# ---------- CONFIG ----------\n",
    "INPUT_DIR = \".\"                      # folder containing your .json files\n",
    "OUTPUT_CSV = \"capex_forecasts.csv\"\n",
    "MODEL = \"claude-sonnet-4-6\"          # current model string;\n",
    "MAX_TOKENS = 500\n",
    "# ----------------------------\n",
    "\n",
    "client = anthropic.Anthropic()       # reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from environment\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def extract_transcript_text(data):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Pull transcript text from common JSON shapes. Adjust to match your files.\"\"\"\n",
    "    if isinstance(data, str):\n",
    "        return data\n",
    "    if isinstance(data, dict):\n",
    "        for key in (\"transcript\", \"text\", \"body\", \"content\", \"components\"):\n",
    "            if key in data:\n",
    "                val = data[key]\n",
    "                if isinstance(val, str):\n",
    "                    return val\n",
    "                if isinstance(val, list):\n",
    "                    parts = []\n",
    "                    for item in val:\n",
    "                        if isinstance(item, str):\n",
    "                            parts.append(item)\n",
    "                        elif isinstance(item, dict):\n",
    "                            for tk in (\"text\", \"value\", \"content\"):\n",
    "                                if tk in item and isinstance(item[tk], str):\n",
    "                                    parts.append(item[tk])\n",
    "                    if parts:\n",
    "                        return \"\\n\".join(parts)\n",
    "        return json.dumps(data)\n",
    "    if isinstance(data, list):\n",
    "        return \"\\n\".join(extract_transcript_text(x) for x in data)\n",
    "    return str(data)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def analyze_transcript(transcript_text):\n",
    "    prompt = PROMPT_TEMPLATE.format(transcript=transcript_text)\n",
    "    message = client.messages.create(\n",
    "        model=MODEL,\n",
    "        max_tokens=MAX_TOKENS,\n",
    "        messages=[{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": prompt}],\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    return message.content[0].text.strip()\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def run_extraction():\n",
    "    results = []\n",
    "    files = sorted(f for f in os.listdir(INPUT_DIR) if f.endswith(\".json\"))\n",
    "    print(f\"Found {len(files)} JSON files.\")\n",
    "    for fname in files:\n",
    "        file_id = os.path.splitext(fname)[0]\n",
    "        path = os.path.join(INPUT_DIR, fname)\n",
    "        print(f\"Processing {file_id} ...\")\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "                data = json.load(f)\n",
    "            transcript_text = extract_transcript_text(data)\n",
    "            answer = analyze_transcript(transcript_text) if transcript_text.strip() else \"no information is provided.\"\n",
    "        except Exception as e:\n",
    "            answer = f\"ERROR: {e}\"\n",
    "        results.append({\"file_id\": file_id, \"response\": answer})\n",
    "        print(f\"  -> {answer[:120]}\")\n",
    "        time.sleep(1)\n",
    "    with open(OUTPUT_CSV, \"w\", newline=\"\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
    "        writer = csv.DictWriter(f, fieldnames=[\"file_id\", \"response\"])\n",
    "        writer.writeheader()\n",
    "        writer.writerows(results)\n",
    "    print(f\"\\nDone. Results saved to {OUTPUT_CSV}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Uncomment to actually run the extraction (requires API key + .json files):\n",
    "# run_extraction()"
   ]
  },
