    "---\n",
    "# Act 2: Measurement: turning words into a number\n",
    "\n",
    "To *test* anything, we need the five text categories as a numeric variable. The natural choice is an **ordinal scale** from −1 to +1:\n",
    "\n",
    "| Text choice | Score |\n",
    "|---|---|\n",
    "| Increase substantially | +1 |\n",
    "| Increase | +0.5 |\n",
    "| No change | 0 |\n",
    "| Decrease | −0.5 |\n",
    "| Decrease substantially | −1 |\n",
    "\n",
    "This mapping looks innocent but bakes in an assumption: that the \"distance\" from *increase* to *increase substantially* equals the distance from *no change* to *increase*. That may or may not be reasonable and it's the kind of choice that may drive results.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "257445da",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "257445da"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "CHOICE_MAP = {\n",
    "    \"increase substantially\": 1,\n",
    "    \"increase\": 0.5,\n",
    "    \"no change\": 0,\n",
    "    \"decrease\": -0.5,\n",
    "    \"decrease substantially\": -1,\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "def parse_choice(text):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Extract the ordinal score from a 'choice - explanation' response.\"\"\"\n",
    "    if not isinstance(text, str):\n",
    "        return np.nan\n",
    "    low = text.strip().lower().replace(\"*\", \"\")\n",
    "    if low.startswith(\"no information\"):\n",
    "        return np.nan\n",
    "    for phrase in sorted(CHOICE_MAP, key=len, reverse=True):   # longest first\n",
    "        if low.startswith(phrase) or phrase in low:\n",
    "            return CHOICE_MAP[phrase]\n",
    "    return np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "signals = pd.read_csv(\"capex_forecasts.csv\")\n",
    "signals[\"signal\"] = signals[\"response\"].apply(parse_choice)\n",
    "SIGNAL_LABELS = {1:\"Increase substantially\", 0.5:\"Increase\", 0:\"No change\",\n",
    "                 -0.5:\"Decrease\", -1:\"Decrease substantially\"}\n",
    "signals[\"signal_label\"] = signals[\"signal\"].map(SIGNAL_LABELS).fillna(\"No information\")\n",
    "signals[[\"file_id\", \"signal\", \"signal_label\"]]"
   ]
  },
