    "---\n",
    "# Act 3: Validation: does the signal predict realized investment?\n",
    "\n",
    "Now we link each firm's signal to its *actual* fiscal-2024 investment from COMPUSTAT and ask whether the late-2023 language had predictive content.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Linking transcripts to COMPUSTAT\n",
    "\n",
    "We use **GVKEY**, COMPUSTAT's permanent firm identifier, the cleanest possible link. You provide a small lookup file, `gvkey_map.csv`, with two columns:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "file_id,gvkey\n",
    "2922311,001234\n",
    "2925229,012345\n",
    "...\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "GVKEYs are 6-digit zero-padded strings in COMPUSTAT (`6066` → `006066`); the code pads them automatically.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "27ebf12b",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "27ebf12b"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "gvmap = pd.read_csv(\"gvkey_map.csv\")          # columns: file_id, gvkey\n",
    "\n",
    "signals[\"file_id\"] = signals[\"file_id\"].astype(str)\n",
    "gvmap[\"file_id\"]   = gvmap[\"file_id\"].astype(str)\n",
    "df_sig = signals.merge(gvmap, on=\"file_id\", how=\"inner\")\n",
    "df_sig[\"gvkey\"] = df_sig[\"gvkey\"].astype(str).str.zfill(6)\n",
    "df_sig[[\"file_id\", \"gvkey\", \"signal\", \"signal_label\"]]"
   ]
