   "source": [
    "### Building the variables\n",
    "\n",
    "## COMPUSTAT variable definitions (`comp.funda`)\n",
    "\n",
    "| Mnemonic | Variable name | Definition |\n",
    "|----------|---------------|------------|\n",
    "| `fyear` | Data Year – Fiscal | The fiscal year the observation covers (not necessarily the calendar year). |\n",
    "| `conm` | Company Name | The company's full legal name. |\n",
    "| `tic` | Ticker Symbol | The exchange ticker symbol for the firm. |\n",
    "| `capx` | Capital Expenditures | Cash outflow for property, plant & equipment; the core investment measure. |\n",
    "| `at` | Assets – Total | Total assets (book value); standard scaling variable for firm size. |\n",
    "| `ppent` | Property, Plant & Equipment – Net | Net (of depreciation) book value of fixed assets; denominator for the investment rate. |\n",
    "| `xrd` | Research & Development Expense | R&D spending expensed during the year (often missing for non-R&D-intensive firms). |\n",
    "| `aqc` | Acquisitions | Cash used for acquisitions during the year (missing/zero when no deals). |\n",
    "| `sale` | Sales / Turnover (Net) | Net revenue / total sales for the period. |\n",
    "| `oancf` | Operating Activities – Net Cash Flow | Cash generated from operations (statement of cash flows). |\n",
    "| `dltt` | Long-Term Debt – Total | Debt due in more than one year. |\n",
    "| `dlc` | Debt in Current Liabilities | Short-term debt and the current portion of long-term debt (due within one year). |\n",
    "| `che` | Cash & Short-Term Investments | Cash and marketable securities; the firm's liquid holdings. |\n",
    "| `csho` | Common Shares Outstanding | Number of common shares outstanding (millions); used with price for market cap. |\n",
    "| `prcc_f` | Price – Close, Fiscal Year-End | Share price at the fiscal year-end close. |\n",
    "| `ceq` | Common/Ordinary Equity – Total | Book value of common equity. |\n",
    "| `txditc` | Deferred Taxes & Investment Tax Credit | Balance-sheet deferred taxes and ITC; added back in the book-equity calc for Tobin's Q. |\n",
    "| `pstkl` | Preferred Stock – Liquidating Value | Liquidating value of preferred stock; subtracted in the book-equity calc for Tobin's Q. |\n",
    "\n",
    "For each firm we compute:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Investment outcomes (FY2024):** capex level, capex growth (24 vs 23), capex/lagged PP&E (the standard *investment rate*), capex/lagged assets.\n",
    "- **Valuation (FY2023):** Tobin's Q = (market equity + total assets − book equity) / total assets. Computed in the *pre-period*, since Q is meant to be a forward-looking predictor — it's the natural benchmark our text signal competes against.\n",
    "- **Financial characteristics (FY2023):** cash flow/assets, leverage, cash/assets, size, sales growth.\n",
    "- **Other channels:** R&D growth, acquisitions/assets.\n",
    "\n",
    "The helper functions below carefully handle missing values (`pd.NA`), which COMPUSTAT has plenty of — not every firm reports R&D or makes acquisitions.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "2e597b1d",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "2e597b1d"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def ok(x):\n",
    "    \"\"\"True only if x is a usable, nonzero number.\"\"\"\n",
    "    return pd.notna(x) and x != 0\n",
    "\n",
    "def build(g):\n",
    "    gv   = g[\"gvkey\"].iloc[0]\n",
    "    conm = g[\"conm\"].iloc[-1]\n",
    "    tic  = g[\"tic\"].iloc[-1]\n",
    "    g = g.set_index(\"fyear\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    def v(y, c):\n",
    "        val = g[c].get(y, np.nan) if c in g.columns else np.nan\n",
    "        return val if pd.notna(val) else np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "    o = {\"gvkey\": gv, \"company\": conm, \"ticker\": tic}\n",
    "    at23, ppe23 = v(2023,\"at\"), v(2023,\"ppent\")\n",
    "    capx23, capx24 = v(2023,\"capx\"), v(2024,\"capx\")\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Investment\n",
    "    o[\"capx_2024\"]      = capx24\n",
    "    o[\"capx_growth\"]    = (capx24/capx23 - 1) if ok(capx23) else np.nan\n",
    "    o[\"capx_to_ppe\"]    = (capx24/ppe23)      if ok(ppe23)  else np.nan\n",
    "    o[\"capx_to_assets\"] = (capx24/at23)       if ok(at23)   else np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Tobin's Q (FY2023)\n",
    "    csho, prcc = v(2023,\"csho\"), v(2023,\"prcc_f\")\n",
    "    me = csho*prcc if (pd.notna(csho) and pd.notna(prcc)) else np.nan\n",
    "    ceq = v(2023,\"ceq\")\n",
    "    be = (ceq if pd.notna(ceq) else np.nan) \\\n",
    "         + (v(2023,\"txditc\") if pd.notna(v(2023,\"txditc\")) else 0) \\\n",
    "         - (v(2023,\"pstkl\")  if pd.notna(v(2023,\"pstkl\"))  else 0)\n",
    "    o[\"tobins_q\"] = ((me + at23 - be)/at23) if (ok(at23) and pd.notna(me) and pd.notna(be)) else np.nan\n",
    "    #Jha et.al. use a more up-to-date defintion of Tobin's q, which includes  intangible capital, measured as externally acquired intangibles (balance sheet), and accumulated R&D expenditures using the perpetual inventory method\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Financial characteristics (FY2023)\n",
    "    o[\"cashflow_to_assets\"] = (v(2023,\"oancf\")/at23) if ok(at23) else np.nan\n",
    "    dltt, dlc = v(2023,\"dltt\"), v(2023,\"dlc\")\n",
    "    debt = (dltt if pd.notna(dltt) else 0) + (dlc if pd.notna(dlc) else 0)\n",
    "    o[\"leverage\"]       = (debt/at23) if ok(at23) else np.nan\n",
    "    o[\"cash_to_assets\"] = (v(2023,\"che\")/at23) if ok(at23) else np.nan\n",
    "    o[\"size_lnassets\"]  = np.log(at23) if (pd.notna(at23) and at23 > 0) else np.nan\n",
    "    sale23 = v(2023,\"sale\")\n",
    "    o[\"sales_growth\"]   = (v(2024,\"sale\")/sale23 - 1) if ok(sale23) else np.nan\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Other investment channels\n",
    "    xrd23 = v(2023,\"xrd\")\n",
    "    o[\"rd_growth\"]     = (v(2024,\"xrd\")/xrd23 - 1) if ok(xrd23) else np.nan\n",
    "    o[\"acq_to_assets\"] = (v(2024,\"aqc\")/at23) if ok(at23) else np.nan\n",
    "    return pd.Series(o)\n",
    "\n",
    "firm = funda.groupby(\"gvkey\", group_keys=False).apply(build).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "firm[\"gvkey\"] = firm[\"gvkey\"].astype(str).str.zfill(6)\n",
    "firm"
   ]
  },
  {
